Representative sample of the repeated tool-level failure encountered while attempting to launch command.txt (this is the Bash tool harness's own error, not a Python traceback from run_experiment.py -- the target process never started):

ENOSPC: no space left on device, open '/private/tmp/claude-501/-Volumes-SSD990-crypto-autoresearcher/655992ba-4699-434f-a2ad-3a4774fe7a8d/tasks/<random>.output'

Observed on the host root filesystem (/dev/disk3s1s1, mounted `/`), which is
also where the Bash tool's own per-invocation output-capture files live
(under /private/tmp/claude-501/...). This repository's own files live on a
separate volume (/Volumes/SSD990), which remained writable throughout via
the Write/Edit/Read tools -- only Bash-tool-mediated command execution
(needed to actually run python3 against run_experiment.py) was blocked.
Independently confirmed as a whole-machine condition by the Coordinator's
own session hitting the identical error at the same time, and escalated by
the Coordinator to the user.
